1
00:03:13,333 --> 00:03:19,333
From comic to screen, discover the making of Marvel's first heroes.

2
00:06:26,666 --> 00:06:32,666
Marvel Studios Assembled: The Making of Eternals is a
documentary film directed by Bradley Hogan.

3
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:46,000
Join director Chloe Zhao and the Cast of Eternals as they recount their experiences
during the making of Marvel Studios’ most ambitious film to date.

4
00:12:53,333 --> 00:12:59,333
Discover how the ensemble cast felt stepping into their roles, filming in remote locations, and creating
bonds that would help to create the on-screen relationships that span over 7,000 years.

5
00:16:06,666 --> 00:16:12,666
Self - Sersi, played by Gemma Chan.

6
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:26,000
Self - Producer, played by Nate Moore.

7
00:22:33,333 --> 00:22:39,333
Self - Dane Whitman, played by Kit Harington.

8
00:25:46,666 --> 00:25:52,666
Self - Kingo, played by Kumail Nanjiani.

9
00:29:00,000 --> 00:29:06,000
Self - Makkari, played by Lauren Ridloff.

10
00:32:13,333 --> 00:32:19,333
Self - Producer, played by Kevin Feige.

11
00:35:26,666 --> 00:35:32,666
Marvel Studios: Assembled is an American anthology television docuseries
of specials created for the streaming service Disney+.

12
00:38:40,000 --> 00:38:46,000
Produced by Marvel Studios, each special goes behind-the-scenes of a Marvel Studios Disney+ series or film, particularly those
within the Marvel Cinematic Universe (MCU), with the creatives, exploring the process of creating each series or film.

13
00:41:53,333 --> 00:41:59,333
The series was first announced in February 2021.

14
00:45:06,666 --> 00:45:12,666
Marvel Studios: Assembled premiered on March 12, 2021, with subsequent specials releasing
shortly after a Disney+ series' completion or a film's Disney+ release.

15
00:48:20,000 --> 00:48:26,000
14 specials were released for Phase Four of the MCU, followed by 9 specials released for Phase Five projects through
2024, including one for the first season of the Marvel Studios Animation series X-Men '97 (2024).

16
00:51:33,333 --> 00:51:39,333
The special for Agatha All Along (2024) was released for free
on Marvel Entertainment's YouTube channel.

17
00:54:46,666 --> 00:54:52,666
Assembled received positive responses for showcasing how each series or film came
together, particularly with the technical aspects and franchise connectivity.
